GHOST — third-party attributions

The numerical core (core/) and the command-line program (native/) are written
from scratch and link no third-party library. The entries below credit
ALGORITHMS and REFERENCE DATA, not copied code, followed by the third-party
packages that the web app and the Manual bundle.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

xoshiro256++ and splitmix64  (core/dae_rng.c)

  Algorithms by David Blackman and Sebastiano Vigna, dedicated to the public
  domain (CC0). https://prng.di.unimi.it/
  The implementation in core/dae_rng.c was written from the published
  description of the algorithms.

Miller's backward recurrence  (core/dae_bessel.c)

  Classical method for Bessel functions of the first kind, normalised by
  J_0(x) + 2 sum_m J_2m(x) = 1. Described in Abramowitz & Stegun, Handbook of
  Mathematical Functions, §9.12, and in Press et al., Numerical Recipes, ch. 6.

Bessel reference table  (native/tests/t00_bessel_table.c)

  Values generated with the Wolfram Language (BesselJ, 30 digits, exact
  rational arguments) and checked independently against mpmath. Test data only;
  not part of the built program.

